#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "provisioning.security"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Product Watcher Permissions
	Testing to assure that provisioning product watcher permissions works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I create a provisioning user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | provisioning.watcher                    |
	| Email Address | provisioning.watcher@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Provisioning                            |
	| Last Name     | Watcher                                 |
	* I assign the provisioning user with the email address "provisioning.watcher@liferay.com.broken" to the provisioning role "Provisioning Watcher"

Teardown:
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| A Visible DXP Product |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| provisioning.watcher@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: View no new product button
	Testing the inability to create products in the provisioning product index 

	Given I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.watcher@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the product index page
	And the new product button should not be present

Scenario: View product
	Testing the ability to view products in the provisioning product index that do not contain a link or delete button

	Given I create a product with the following values
	| Name | A Visible DXP Product | |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.watcher@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a non linked product on the provisioning index with the name "A Visible DXP Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Visible DXP Product |
	And the delete button for the product "A Visible DXP Product" should not be present